@2:21 the new alignment things for the booster stand are interesting, but also different it seems than whats on the OLP...

The White/grey right by the SpaceX worker is a ram that seems to allow for the whole guide assembly to move up and down (explains the cable snakes seen in the next shot) so it seems they would be raised up when the booser is being lowered, engage with the sockets on the booster when its still mostly above the stand, then lower with the booster keeping it fully rotationally alligned and alligend horizontally with respect to the stand allowing the for a much much quicker lowering process as it get close to the stand (as the booster could not rotate very much, nor move horizontally very much meaning its just a case of keep lowering until it engages the lock...)

As far as we've seen the OLP pins don't have the ability to raise and lower... but who knows!

@NasaSpaceflight video idea: I mentioned this in SBL during the eclipse but I think I should put it here too.

At the end of each month/year/whenever, there should be a contemplation video of cool nature things that have occurred on SBL i.e shooting stars, Boca Chica Airforce (The ginormus swarm of birds from a while ago), lightning storms, nilgai and coyote walking around Starbase, !Bird from booster 7 testing, the Lunar Eclipse, etc.

Videos like this could bring people with different interests to the channel and inevitably get more people interested in SpaceX/rockets. Just some food for thought!

@Mary on her Birthday.  Though we don’t hear so much anymore “Mary up at dawn capturing the sunrise, on the hill in sweltering sun, at dusk swatting Texas mosquitos,” your unflagging silently, professionally, recording space history at Boca Chica is remembered and apppreciated by all us tank watchers.

Cheers to many more Happy Birthdays Mary.
