for anyone wondering about artemis III updates, there was a tour of stennis where they had a Q&A time. here’s some things we learned:

nasa says crew selection is dependent on which HLS is flown. there is one crew more accustomed to starship, and another for blue moon. until they know that, they cannot announce crew.

nasa has one upper stage left of the current design (ICPS). engineers are currently assessing if the upper stage is necessary for the launch or if it should be saved for artemis IV. it depends highly on the energy (altitude) of the orbit.
